1	# mcp-db-server
2	
3	[![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-Apache%202.0-blue.svg)](https://opensource.org/licenses/Apache-2.0)
4	[![Python](https://img.shields.io/badge/python-3.11+-blue.svg)](https://www.python.org/downloads/)
5	
6	An MCP (Model Context Protocol) server that exposes relational databases (PostgreSQL/MySQL) to AI agents with natural language query support. Transform natural language questions into SQL queries and get structured results.
7	
8	## Features
9	
10	- **Multi-Database Support**: Works with PostgreSQL and MySQL
11	- **Natural Language to SQL**: Convert plain English queries to SQL using HuggingFace transformers
12	- **RESTful API**: Clean FastAPI-based endpoints for database operations
13	- **Safety First**: Read-only operations with query validation and result limits
14	- **Docker Ready**: Complete containerization with Docker Compose
15	- **Production Ready**: Health checks, logging, and error handling
16	- **AI Agent Friendly**: Designed specifically for AI agent integration
17	
18	## API Endpoints
19	
20	| Endpoint                          | Method | Description                                  |
21	| --------------------------------- | ------ | -------------------------------------------- |
22	| `/health`                         | GET    | Health check and service status              |
23	| `/mcp/list_tables`                | GET    | List all available tables with column counts |
24	| `/mcp/describe/{table_name}`      | GET    | Get detailed schema for a specific table     |
25	| `/mcp/query`                      | POST   | Execute natural language queries             |
26	| `/mcp/tables/{table_name}/sample` | GET    | Get sample data from a table                 |
27	
28	## Quick Start
29	
30	### Option 1: Docker Compose (Recommended)
31	
32	1. **Clone and start the services:**
33	
34	   ```bash
35	   git clone https://github.com/Souhar-dya/mcp-db-server.git
36	   cd mcp-db-server
37	   docker-compose up --build
38	   ```
39	
40	2. **Test the endpoints:**
41	
42	   ```bash
43	   # Health check
44	   curl http://localhost:8000/health
45	
46	   # List tables
47	   curl http://localhost:8000/mcp/list_tables
48	
49	   # Describe a table
50	   curl http://localhost:8000/mcp/describe/customers
51	
52	   # Natural language query
53	   curl -X POST "http://localhost:8000/mcp/query" \
54	     -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
55	     -d '{"nl_query": "show top 5 customers by total orders"}'
56	   ```
57	
58	### Option 2: Local Development
59	
60	1. **Prerequisites:**
61	
62	   - Python 3.11+
63	   - PostgreSQL or MySQL database
64	
65	2. **Install dependencies:**
66	
67	   ```bash
68	   pip install -r requirements.txt
69	   ```
70	
71	3. **Set environment variables:**
72	
73	   ```bash
74	   export DATABASE_URL="postgresql+asyncpg://user:password@localhost:5432/dbname"
75	   # or for MySQL:
76	   # export DATABASE_URL="mysql+pymysql://user:password@localhost:3306/dbname"
77	   ```
78	
